language en
lemma about
license
  name "CC BY 4.0"
  url "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/"
senses
  entry
    definition "(of quantities) imprecise but fairly close to correct"
    examples ("lasted approximately an hour" "in just about a minute" "he's about 30 years old" "I've had about all I can stand" "we meet about once a month" "some forty people came" "weighs around a hundred pounds" "roughly $3,000" "holds 3 gallons, more or less" "20 or so people were at the party")
    id oewn-00007414-r
    partOfSpeech r
    synonyms (approximately "close to" "just about" some roughly "more or less" around "or so")
  entry
    definition "all around or on all sides"
    examples ("dirty clothes lying around (or about)" "let's look about for help" "There were trees growing all around" "she looked around her")
    id oewn-00072240-r
    partOfSpeech r
    synonyms (around)
  entry
    definition "in the area or vicinity"
    examples ("a few spectators standing about" "hanging around" "waited around for the next flight")
    id oewn-00071565-r
    partOfSpeech r
    synonyms (around)
  entry
    definition "used of movement to or among many different places or in no particular direction"
    examples ("wandering about with no place to go" "people were rushing about" "news gets around (or about)" "traveled around in Asia" "he needs advice from someone who's been around" "she sleeps around")
    id oewn-00072729-r
    partOfSpeech r
    synonyms (around)
  entry
    definition "in or to a reversed position or direction"
    examples ("about face" "suddenly she turned around")
    id oewn-00072601-r
    partOfSpeech r
    synonyms (around)
  entry
    definition "in rotation or succession"
    examples ("turn about is fair play")
    id oewn-00359910-r
    partOfSpeech r
  entry
    definition "(of actions or states) slightly short of or not quite accomplished; all but"
    examples ("the job is (just) about done" "the baby was almost asleep when the alarm sounded" "we're almost finished" "the car all but ran her down" "he nearly fainted" "talked for nigh onto 2 hours" "the recording is well-nigh perfect" "virtually all the parties signed the contract" "I was near exhausted by the run" "most everyone agrees")
    id oewn-00073433-r
    partOfSpeech r
    synonyms (almost most nearly near nigh virtually well-nigh)
  entry
    definition "on the move"
    examples ("up and about" "the whole town was astir over the incident")
    id oewn-00032471-s
    partOfSpeech s
    synonyms (astir)
